  sources:
  - name: Mainzer Fernwaerme KWK-Anlagendaten 2021-2025
    authority: Mainzer Fernwaerme GmbH, ueber Mainzer Stadtwerke AG
    url:
    description: "Annual CHP electricity for the Mainz district heating plants (KW3,
      KW5, the KW3 steam share, MHKW and TVM), 2021-2025. The sheet offers gross and
      net generation and provisional and final CHP electricity; the utility states
      which applies: 'zgl. der Bilanzierung unserer FW-Emissionen/dem PEF verwende
      ich gemaess der Berechnungsmethoden den endgueltigen KWK-Strom Netto'. That
      figure divided by itself plus the delivered heat gives the electricity fraction
      the exergetic allocation needs: 0.427 (2021), 0.395 (2022), 0.330 (2023), 0.334
      (2024) - against the shared template's placeholder of 0.30. TVM's net figures
      for 2022-2024 are MWh written into a kWh column (965/747/612 against 8.7-9.6
      million kWh gross); the 2025 row confirms the ratio at about 11 percent either
      way. Corrected on read; TVM is 0.3 percent of the total. The supply temperature
      is given as a range, 90-115 C by season, and therefore lives as a slider parameter
      on the node rather than in this dataset. The delivery starts in 2021, so 2019
      and 2020 are left empty for the node to extend. Note the utility also says the
      Carnot method is maintained 'nur informatorisch' for now and becomes binding
      for district heating only during the coming year.; Format: .xlsx; Licensing:
      Provided to the city for climate accounting; not public; Geographic Coverage:
      Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Annual; Date Last Updated: 2026-08-24;
      Updated by: Mainzer Fernwaerme GmbH"
  units:
    electricity_fraction: ''
